er\\\",\\n                      \\\"workflow_type\\\": \\\"prototype\\\",\\n                      \\\"workflow_id\\\": \\\"35\\\",\\n                      \\\"workflow_run_id\\\": \\\"7c8f59d5282d4b9c859696f4084d0223\\\"\\n                    },\\n                    \\\"data\\\": \\\"626130f7c71f6b9e651c76be/69be3b4593ce5ab1f19b2cfb/file_9---22d160af-8b90-4476-8931-ac57b0b9876d.jpg\\\",\\n                    \\\"pdf_path\\\": null\\n                  }\\n                },\\n                \\\"node_name_dict\\\": \\\"NodeDataReader5\\\",\\n                \\\"executed\\\": \\\"completed\\\",\\n                \\\"node_id\\\": \\\"6936866fb56d784128f48718\\\",\\n                \\\"prototype_id\\\": \\\"69be3b4593ce5ab1f19b2cfb\\\"\\n              }\\n            ]\\n          }\\n        ],\\n        \\\"external_nodes\\\": []\\n      }\\n    ],\\n    \\\"project_link_id\\\": \\\"\\\",\\n    \\\"concert_hall_id\\\": \\\"627392cbef51f1256835d0e8\\\",\\n    \\\"session_id\\\": \\\"a3pheusuepvmgzkkfdvwgq\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"analyzer_image_url\\\": null,\\n  \\\"sent_result_image\\\": false,\\n  \\\"local_image_path_used\\\": \\\"/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/file_9---22d160af-8b90-4476-8931-ac57b0b9876d.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"telegram_user_id_used_for_upload\\\": \\\"495506013\\\",\\n  \\\"upload_path\\\": \\\"upload/2026-03-31_13.32.26_kBRhBptTc6MqF4Flk70D/\\\",\\n  \\\"upload_filename\\\": \\\"file_9---22d160af-8b90-4476-8931-ac57b0b9876d.jpg\\\",\\n  \\\"upload_request_url\\\": \\\"http://looporchestra.sytes.net:4001/nodes/input/upload?storage_ref=nodes_bucket&local_file_path=upload%2F&user_id=495506013\\\",\\n  \\\"raw_upload_response\\\": {\\n    \\\"path\\\": \\\"upload/2026-03-31_13.32.26_kBRhBptTc6MqF4Flk70D/\\\",\\n    \\\"filename\\\": \\\"file_9---22d160af-8b90-4476-8931-ac57b0b9876d.jpg\\\",\\n    \\\"column_names\\\": null\\n  }\\n}\",\"cwd\":\"/home/node/.openclaw/workspace\"},\"isError\":false,\"timestamp\":1774963961578}}\n/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json.bak.2:94:          \"skin-cancer-pipeline\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/SOUL.md:47:- If the Patient Agent forwards a request to run the skin cancer pipeline, together with a CT scan, run the \"skin-cancer-pipeline\" skill.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/SOUL.md:48:- Based on the output of the skin cancer skill, rework it based on your expertise, and return the result to the Patient Agent.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/TOOLS.md:54:## skin-cancer-pipeline\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/TOOLS.md:55:- **Role:** Execute the fixed skin cancer detection pipeline starting from a skin image file.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/TOOLS.md:56:- **Use for:** running the integrated skin pipeline when an image should be uploaded and passed through the Skin Cancer Detection model, the Image Analyzer component, and the downstream X-AI component.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/TOOLS.md:58:- **Meaning:** Produces a preliminary pipeline result structure; for quick summaries, prioritize these wanted outputs when present: the skin cancer class, the skin cancer confidence, the Image Analyzer prediction, and all available `cam_...` fields from the Image Analyzer output, especially the full `cam_metrics` set and `cam_explanation`.\n/home/node/.openclaw/workspace-doctor-agent-2/TOOLS.md:59:- **Presentation rule:** When reporting results to the user, do not default to low-level JSON labels. Present them in a cleaner summary with readable labels such as `Skin cancer class`, `Confidence`, `Image Analyzer prediction`, `CAM coverage`, `CAM center ratio`, `CAM left-right asymmetry`, `CAM top-bottom asymmetry`, and `CAM explanation`.\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/references/request-template.json:74:                           \"node_label\":\"Skin Cancer Detection\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/references/request-template.json:75:                           \"node_description\":\"Skin Cancer Detection\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/references/request-template.json:79:                                 \"endpoint\":\"/nodes/ai_tool/skin-cancer-detection-model\"\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/SKILL.md:2:name: skin-cancer-pipeline\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/SKILL.md:3:description: Execute the skin cancer image pipeline by uploading a user-provided skin image through the same upload endpoint used by the kidney pipeline, taking the real uploaded image path returned by that endpoint, replacing the image-path placeholders inside the fixed skin-cancer prototype request JSON, then sending the built request to the same prototype execution endpoint and returning the pipeline response plus any analyzer image URL for normal chat forwarding. Use when a user wants to run the integrated skin-cancer pipeline on an uploaded image and inspect either the raw response or a clean summary of the main outputs.\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/SKILL.md:6:# Skin Cancer Pipeline\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/SKILL.md:8:Upload the user image first, use the returned upload path in the fixed request template, then execute the skin-cancer pipeline.\n/home/node/.openclaw/skills/skin-cancer-pipeline/SKILL.md:64:### Skin Cancer Detection\n/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json.bak.1:94:          \"skin-cancer-pipeline\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/openclaw.json.bak.1:424:          \"skin-cancer-pipeline\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/SkinCancer---9cb0f1f0-05fc-4432-b272-ac7c682bc4ac.json:74:                           \"node_label\":\"Skin Cancer Detection\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/SkinCancer---9cb0f1f0-05fc-4432-b272-ac7c682bc4ac.json:75:                           \"node_description\":\"Skin Cancer Detection\",\n/home/node/.openclaw/media/inbound/SkinCancer---9cb0f1f0-05fc-4432-b272-ac7c682bc4ac.json:79:                                 \"end